<td><h2>SAGA OIL ASA - Production Update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2009-03-13 14:00:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 13.Mars, 2009)<br><br>SAGA Oil sold 5 430 barrels of crude oil in February.<br><br>PROMGEOTEK conducted a workover operation on the well 106 in the<br>period mid-January to end of February. Production from the well 106<br>commenced 1 March 2009, with a production of 150 barrels per. day. An<br>increase of 50 barrels per day.  The average production to date in<br>March is 270 barrels per day.<br><br><br>About SAGA Oil ASA<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA was established in October 2005 to focus on exploration,<br>development and production of oil and gas assets in Russia. SAGA Oil<br>currently holds two production licenses in Orenburg region through<br>its Russian subsidiary.<br><br>SAGA Oil has it's headquarter in Stavanger, Norway, and has around 60<br>employees in Norway and Russia. The company's shares are listed at<br>the OTC market (Over the Counter-List) in Oslo, Norway.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO John Arne Farstad,  + 47 51 63 08 00, email:<br>jaf@sagaoil.no<br><br><br>This announcement was originally distributed by Hugin. The issuer is <br>solely responsible for the content of this announcement.</p></td>
</tr>
