<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA - Financial Update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-12-19 16:00:03</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 19. December, 2008)<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA has for some time been in a very difficult cash<br>situation and has negotiated with its creditors for a creditor<br>agreement.<br><br>The SAGA Oil group has now  received some cash through a VAT refund<br>in Russia. This gives the company means to sign a creditor agreement<br>with the financial creditors. The agreement will give the company<br>some time to realize its assets or find other solutions acceptable to<br>the creditors.<br><br>The board member Milana Zubairaeva, living in Russia, has informed<br>the board that she wishes to resign as a board member. The board are<br>working to find her replacement.<br><br><br>About SAGA Oil ASA<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA was established in October 2005 to focus on exploration,<br>development and production of oil and gas assets in Russia. SAGA Oil<br>currently holds two production licenses in Orenburg region through<br>its Russian subsidiary.<br><br>SAGA Oil has it's headquarter in Stavanger, Norway, and has around 60<br>employees in Norway and Russia. The company's shares are listed at<br>the OTC market (Over the Counter-List) in Oslo, Norway.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Lasse K Fjell,  +47 51 63 08 00, email:<br>lf@sagaoil.no<br><br><br>This announcement was originally distributed by Hugin. The issuer is <br>solely responsible for the content of this announcement.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1279005/285472.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1279005/285472.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA - Finansiell Oppdatering</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-12-19 16:00:03</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 19. desember, 2008)<br><br><br>Saga Oil ASA har i lengre tid hatt svært stram likviditet og har<br>forhandlet med kreditorene om en kreditoravtale.<br><br>Konsernet er nå tilført noe likviditet gjennom refusjon av<br>merverdiavgift i Russland. Dette gir grunnlag for inngåelse av<br>kreditoravtale med de finansielle kreditorene. Avtalen vil<br>forutsetningsvis gi selskapet ro i en periode med sikte på å<br>realisere selskapets eiendeler eller eventuelt finne andre løsninger<br>som er akseptable for kreditorene.<br><br>Styremedlemmet Milana Zubairaeva, bosatt i Russland, har meddelt at<br>hun ønsker å trekke seg fra sitt verv og selskapet arbeider for å<br>finne en erstatter for henne.<br><br><br>Om SAGA Oil ASA<br>SAGA Oil ASA ble etablert i oktober 2005 for å fokusere på leting,<br>utvikling og produksjon av olje og gass i Russland. SAGA Oil eier<br>gjennom et russisk datterselskap to produksjonslisenser i<br>Orenburg-regionen i Russland.<br><br>SAGA Oil har hovedkontor i Stavanger, Norge, og har rundt 60 ansatte<br>i Norge og Russland. Selskapets aksjer omsettes på Norsk Fondsmegler<br>Forbunds "Over the Counter-List" (OTC).<br><br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt:<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Lasse K Fjell,  + 47 51 63 08 00, email:<br>lf@sagaoil.no<br><br><br>Informasjonen er distribuert av Hugin.</p></td>
</tr>
