<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Production update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-08-22 15:30:03</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 22August, 2008)<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA sold 3 400 barrels of oil in July.<br><br>The new management have after its entrance in the company median<br>July, initiated a process of evaluation of current status, and<br>necessary actions to raise production from the company's existing<br>wells. Additionally an evaluation of the drilling campaign is<br>ongoing. The new management focus on putting existing wells in<br>production, and has ambitions to produce from 14 wells year end. In<br>connection with the refinancing of the company, the management will<br>present production estimates for the company's oil and gas licenses.<br><br>In connection with the ongoing refinancing of SAGA Oil ASA, the<br>company has been approached by several parties regarding structural<br>transactions and strategic co operation. The company has initiated<br>discussions with some of the parties. SEB Enskilda is the company's<br>advisor in this process.<br><br>The company urges existing and future shareholders to thoroughly<br>investigate the financial situation of the company. Further<br>information regarding the financial situation can be obtained by<br>contacting the company.<br><br>About SAGA Oil ASA<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA was established in October 2005 to focus on exploration,<br>development and production of oil and gas assets in Russia and the<br>FSU. The company's founder has more than 20 years of business<br>experience in the Soviet Union and Russia. SAGA Oil currently holds<br>two production licenses in Orenburg region through its Russian<br>subsidiary. The company started production from the first license in<br>2007, and it will gradually build up its production during 2008 and<br>will start developing its new acreage.<br>SAGA Oil has it's headquarter in Stavanger, Norway, and has around 80<br>employees in Norway and Russia. The company's shares are listed at<br>the OTC market (Over the Counter-List) in Oslo, Norway.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1245641/269081.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1245641/269081.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA: Innkalling til ekstraordinær generalforsamling i Saga<br>Oil ASA</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-08-18 15:00:03</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Det innkalles herved til generalforsamling i Saga Oil ASA, den 1.<br>september 2008 kl 1700 i selskapets lokaler i Maskinveien 24 i<br>Stavanger.<br><br>Generalforsamlingen åpnes av styrets leder Stig Hetlevik.<br><br>Styret har fastlagt slikt forslag til dagsorden:<br><br><br> 1. Valg av møteleder og representant til å medundertegne protokollen<br>    sammen med møteleder<br> 1. Godkjennelse av innkalling og dagsorden<br> 1. Presisering av vedtak om frittståendetegningsretter<br> 1. Valg av styremedlemmer<br><br><br>Aksjonærene bes om å returnere vedlagte<br>påmeldingsskjema/fullmaktsskjema i utfylt stand, innen 27. august<br>2008, til Saga Oil ASA v/Lasse Fjell via telefax +47 5163 0799, per<br>post til Saga Oil ASA, Maskinveien 24, 4033 Stavanger eller e-post<br>lasse.fjell@sagaoil.no.<br><br><br>                     Stavanger, 18. august 2008<br><br>                   _______________________________<br>                            Stig Hetlevik<br>                            styrets leder<br><br><br>Vedlegg:<br><br> 1. Til sak 3 og 4<br> 1. Påmeldings- / fullmaktsskjema</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
