<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Bond Loan in SAGA Oil ASA</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-07-11 16:20:03</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, July 11, 2008)<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA has initiated negotiations with Norsk Tillitsmann to<br>extend the maturity date of  ISIN NO 001 032 223.3 12.00 per cent<br>SAGA Oil ASA Bond Issue 2006/2008 Call and Warrants maturing 14th of<br>July 2008. The background for these negotiations are that SAGA Oil<br>ASA has not yet completed its ongoing financing process and is<br>therefore not in a position to repay the bond loan on the maturity<br>date. SAGA Oil ASA will provide further information in due course.<br><br><br>About SAGA Oil ASA<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA was established in October 2005 to focus on exploration,<br>development and production of oil and gas assets in Russia and the<br>FSU. The company's founder has more than 20 years of business<br>experience in the Soviet Union and Russia. SAGA Oil currently holds<br>two production licenses in Orenburg region through its Russian<br>subsidiary. The company started production from the first license in<br>2007, and it will gradually build up its production during 2008 and<br>will start developing its new acreage.<br>SAGA Oil has it's headquarter in Stavanger, Norway, and has around 80<br>employees in Norway and Russia. The company's shares are listed at<br>the OTC market (Over the Counter-List) in Oslo, Norway.<br><br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>Stig Hetlevik cell.nr: +47 905 90 967<br>Chairman of the Board SAGA Oil ASA</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1235477/263369.pdf">
