<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA - SAGA OIL wins court case for the right to use the SAGA<br>name</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-04-02 09:20:05</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Stavanger, March, 28th, 2008: SAGA Oil ASA has won a clear victory<br>over Statoil Hydro for the right to use the name SAGA. This is stated<br>by Borgarting Lagmannsrett (Norwegian Court of Appeal) in their<br>ruling.<br>In 2006 SAGA Oil instituted legal proceedings against Norsk Hydro to<br>make them remove the SAGA trade marks from the  Trade mark Registry.<br>This was a response to Hydro's indictment against SAGA Oil for the<br>use of the name SAGA. After this ruling, Statoil Hydro has lost in<br>two judicial authorities.<br><br>- We have always believed we had the right to use the name SAGA, and<br>we are of course very happy that the ruling in the Court of Appeal<br>was  unanimously concluded in our favour, says the SAGA Oil ASA CEO<br>Malvin Hoeydal , and adds:<br>- This is an important principal  judicial decision, as it states<br>that a brand name must be actively in use for the brand owner to keep<br>his exclusive right  to a brand name. As a brand owner, he cannot<br>passively block others to develop their markets. We hope this<br>judgment will be final and hopefully it will be of help also for<br>other companies.<br><br>SAGA Oil was established in 2005 to focus on the large oil and gas<br>industry in Russia. As the SAGA name had not been in use in the oil<br>industry for many years, the company founders have chosen this name<br>with its roots back to the Viking age, to illustrate the strong<br>Norwegian tradition in doing business with Russia.<br><br>SAGA Oil owns and operates an oil field in Orenburg region in Russia,<br>and has just bought an additional oil and gas license in the same<br>area. The company develops fast and by now owns oil and gas resaves<br>of  more than100 million barrels of oil equivalents. The company's<br>production is  in the initial  stage and SAGA Oil expects to produce<br>some 3,500 barrels of oil at the end of 2008.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>Malvin Hoeydal, CEO, +47 97422959<br><br><br>About SAGA Oil ASA<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA was established in October 2005 to focus on exploration,<br>development and production of oil and gas assets in Russia and the<br>FSU. The company's founder has more than 20 years of business<br>experience in the Soviet Union and Russia. SAGA Oil currently holds<br>two production licenses in Orenburg region  through its Russian<br>subsidiary. The company started production from the first license in<br>2007, and it will gradually build up its production during 2008 and<br>will start developing its new acreage.<br>SAGA Oil has it's headquarter in Stavanger, Norway, and has around 80<br>employees in Norway and Russia. The company's shares are listed at<br>the OTC market in Oslo, Norway.<br><br>For more information, please visit:<br>www.sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1205648/247774.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1205648/247774.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA - SAGA Oil fikk fullt medhold i sak om rett til bruken<br>av SAGA-navnet</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-04-02 09:20:04</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Stavanger, 28. mars, 2008: SAGA Oil har vunnet en klar seier over<br>StatoilHydro om retten til å bruke SAGA-navnet. Det slår Borgarting<br>Lagmannsrett fast i sin kjennelse. Det var SAGA Oil som i 2006 tok ut<br>søksmål mot Norsk Hydro ASA med krav om å slette de registrerte SAGA-<br>varemerkene i Varemerkeregistret. Søksmålet var et svar på Hydros<br>foretaksnavnklage mot SAGA Oil. Etter kjennelsen fra lagmannsretten<br>har statsoljeselskapet tapt i to rettsinnstanser.<br><br>- Vi har hele tiden ment at vi hadde rett til å bruke SAGA-navnet, og<br>vi er selvsagt meget tilfreds med at lagmannsretten så entydig<br>konkluderer i vår favør, sier administrerende direktør Malvin Høydal<br>i SAGA Oil ASA og fortsetter:<br>- Det er også en viktig prinsipiell dom da den slår fast at<br>varemerkene skal brukes aktivt for at eier skal kunne opprettholde<br>sine enerettigheter i forhold til et merke, og ikke sitte som passiv<br>merkeinnehaver å blokkere for andres markedsutvikling. Vi håper denne<br>dommen nå blir stående, og at den kan være til hjelp for andre<br>selskaper.<br><br>SAGA Oil ble etablert i 2005 som det første Norske  selskap som<br>satser på olje og gass næringen i Russland. Etter at SAGA-navnet ikke<br>hadde vært brukt innen oljeindustrien gjennom en årrekke valgte<br>etablererne dette navnet med røtter tilbake i vikingtiden for å<br>illustrere Norges sterke handelstradisjoner med Russland.<br><br>SAGA Oil har et felt i operasjon i Orenburg-regionen i Russland, og<br>kjøpte nylig en lovende lisens i det samme området. Selskapet er i<br>hurtig vekst og  har over 100 millioner fat oljereserver. Selskapets<br>oljeproduksjon er under oppbygging og SAGA Oil regner med å produsere<br>rundt 3 500 fat olje per dag ved utgangen av 2008.<br><br>For ytterligere informasjon:<br>Malvin Høydal, Adm. dir, +47 974 22 959<br><br><br>Om SAGA Oil ASA<br>SAGA Oil ASA ble etablert i oktober 2005 for å fokusere på leting,<br>utvikling og produksjon av olje og gass i Russland og tidligere<br>Sovjetunionen. Selskapets grunnlegger har mer enn 20 års<br>foretningserfaring innen petroleum industrien fra Russland og<br>tidligere Sovjetunionen. SAGA Oil eier gjennom et russisk<br>datterselskap to produksjonslisenser i Orenburg-regionen i Russland.<br>Selskapet startet produksjon fra den første lisensen i 2007 og vil i<br>løpet av 2008 gradvis øke produksjonen og utvikle det nye  lisens<br>areal. SAGA Oil har hovedkontor i Stavanger, Norge, og har rundt 80<br>ansatte i Norge og Russland. Selskapets aksjer omsettes på Norsk<br>Fondsmegler Forbunds "over the counter-list" (OTC).<br><br>For mer informasjon, besøk:<br>www.sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1205647/247773.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1205647/247773.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA: fourth quarter 2007 report</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2008-03-10 17:00:03</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Stavanger, 10 March 2008: During the fourth quarter of 2007 SAGA Oil<br>reached an important milestone starting commercial production of oil<br>from its Russian operation. In addition focus has been on continuing<br>the drilling program and on well completion to build up production.<br>SAGA Oil also entered into agreements regarding sale of oil and going<br>into 2008 the company is well positioned to grow its Russian<br>operations both in terms of production as well as financially.<br><br>During the fourth quarter two exploration wells were drilled on the<br>Petrovsky field, confirming that the preliminary 6.4 million BOE<br>extractable recourses are in place. To further accelerate SAGA Oil's<br>growth, the company in February entered into agreement to purchase<br>the 637 square kilometre Kudryashovsky license in the Russian<br>Orenburg region. The license has preliminary extractable reserves of<br>60.8 million BOE, confirmed by the Russian state. Combined with the<br>positive development seen during the fourth quarter it provides<br>valuable experience and establishes SAGA Oil as a player in the<br>emerging Russian oil and gas market.<br><br>"We are pleased with the development seen during the fourth quarter<br>and the basis it has formed for future growth. However, the start of<br>2008 has not been according to plan, but these problems have been<br>solved and we expect production to pick up significantly during March<br>and the spring. Through the acquisition of new acreage we also form a<br>solid basis for future growth both in reserves and production" says<br>President & CEO Malvin Høydal.<br><br>The company had revenues of NOK 2.00 million (NOK 2.68million) in the<br>fourth quarter and a negative operating result of NOK 18.1 million<br>(NOK 6.6 million) in the period. The results reflect the generally<br>higher activity and cost level preparing for production start-up.<br>SAGA Oil expects revenues to increase going forward.<br><br>During the first two months of 2008 external factors have slowed down<br>SAGA Oil's oil production. Extreme weather conditions with strong<br>winds and temperatures below -35 Celsius led to work on the wells<br>slowing down and overall causing delays. However, these temporary<br>problems have now been solved and the company expects further<br>positive development over the coming months. The company produced<br>12,150 barrels of oil in January and 4,311 barrels of oil in February<br>and expects to increase the production significantly during the<br>coming months. SAGA Oil has set a production target of 3,500 barrels<br>a day by the end of 2008.<br><br>Quarterly report attached<br>Company presentation will be available on www.sagaoil.no<br><br>For further information:<br>Malvin Høydal, President & CEO<br><br>Tel: +47 51 63 08 00<br>Mob: +47 97 42 29 59<br><br>Or visit www.sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1199656/244822.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1199656/244822.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
