<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA - Operational update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-12-05 07:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger December 5. 2006)<br><br>RIG #1: Reached total depth on well #103<br>Rig 1 has now reached total depth of 2250 meters on well #103.<br>Currently well #103 is undergoing conditioning and logging.<br>Thereafter running in casing and cementing before the Rig is moved<br>and wells #102 and #103 are prepared for completion and start of<br>production.<br><br>RIG #2: Drilling at 1440 meters on well #106<br>Rig 2 is currently drilling at 1440 meters at well #106, and the plan<br>is to drill down to a total depth of 2100 meters in order to assess<br>the reserves on the perimeter of the northern border of the license.<br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 97422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091475/192516.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091475/192516.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Organisatorisk oppdatering</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-12-05 07:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 5. desember 2006)<br><br>Thor Jensen ansatt som direktør for Boreoperasjoner<br>SAGA Oil ASA kan med glede informere om at Thor Jensen er ansatt som<br>Direktør for Boreoperasjoner for å styrke selskapets ledelse innen<br>boreaktiviteter. Thor Jensen har over 30 års erfaring fra arbeid som<br>senior Boresjef i flere norske og internasjonale boreselskaper både<br>nasjonalt og internasjonalt.<br><br>Thor vil inngå i SAGA Oils ledelse med ansvar for å etablere og<br>implementere en ny og moderne boreledelse i Russland som skal sikre<br>og optimalisere SAGA Oil's omfattende boreprogram på Rodnikovsky<br>lisensen.<br><br><br>SAGA Oil ASA vinner frem i søksmål mot Norsk Hydro ASA<br>Oslo Tingrett fastslo den 29. november 2006 at Hydros registrerte<br>Saga-varemerker skal slettes fra Varemerkeregisteret. Saga Oil ASA<br>fikk fullt medhold i sin påstand om at Hydro ikke har brukt<br>Saga-varemerkene de siste fem år. Hydro må også dekke Saga Oil ASAs<br>saksomkostninger.<br><br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Malvin Høydal, mob: +47 974 22 959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 928 05 787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091477/192517.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091477/192517.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Saga Oil ASA - Organisational update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-12-05 07:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger December 5. 2006)<br><br>Mr. Thor Jensen employed as Vice President Drilling Operations<br><br>SAGA Oil ASA has the great pleasure to announce that Mr. Thor Jensen<br>has been appointed Vice President Drilling Operations in order to<br>strengthen the SAGA management in drilling activities. Mr. Jensen has<br>had a long and successful national and international career working<br>as a Senior Drilling Manager in several Norwegian and International<br>drilling companies for more than 3 decades.<br><br>Mr. Jensen has now joined SAGA Oil ASA as Vice President Drilling<br>Operations with responsibility for creating and implementing a new<br>and modern drilling management in Russia, to safeguard and to<br>optimize SAGA Oil's extensive drilling campaign on the Rodnikovsky<br>license.<br><br><br>SAGA Oil ASA wins law suit versus Norsk Hydro ASA<br>On 29 November 2006 Oslo City Court ruled that Hydro's registered<br>trademarks protecting SAGA-trademarks shall be deleted from the<br>Trademark Register. The Court sustained Saga Oil ASA's claim that<br>Hydro had not complied with the requirement regarding "genuine use"<br>of the trademarks during the last five years. Hydro was also ordered<br>to cover Saga Oil ASA's legal expenses.<br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 97422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091478/192518.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091478/192518.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Operasjonell oppdatering</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-12-05 07:10:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 5. desember 2006)<br><br>RIGG #1: Nådd total dybde på brønn #103<br>Rigg 1 har nå nådd total dybde ved 2250 meter på brønn #103. Brønnen<br>blir nå kondisjonert, og det vil deretter gjennomføres logging før<br>det kjøres inn fôringsrør og sementeres. Riggen vil deretter flyttes<br>og brønnene #102 og #103 vil forberedes for komplettering og<br>produksjonsstart.<br><br>RIGG #2: Borer på 1440 meter ved brønn #106<br>Rigg 2 borer videre ved 1440 meter på brønn #106, og det er planlagt<br>å bore ned til en total dybde på 2100 meter for å verifisere<br>reservene som finnes i avgrensings område på nordsiden av lisensen.<br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Malvin Høydal, mob: +47 974 22 959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 928 05 787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091473/192515.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1091473/192515.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA- Financial update: registered increase in share capital</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-16 10:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger November 16. 2006) As reported in the Company's<br>notification on 3 November 2006, the Board of Directors in SAGA Oil<br>ASA has resolved to increase the share capital by the issuance of<br>18 944 821 new shares. The share capital increase has been registered<br>in the Register for Business Enterprises (Foretaksregisteret). The<br>new share capital of SAGA Oil ASA is NOK 4 546 757.12 divided into<br>56 834 464 shares, each with a nominal value of NOK 0.08.<br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 97422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Finansiell oppdatering: registrert kapitalforhøyelse</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-16 10:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 16. november 2006) Som det fremgikk av selskapets melding<br>av 3. november 2006, har styret i SAGA Oil besluttet å øke selskapets<br>aksjekapital ved utstedelse av 18 944 821 nye aksjer. Denne<br>aksjekapitalforhøyelsen er blitt registrert i Foretaksregisteret.<br>SAGA Oil ASAs nye aksjekapital er NOK 4 546 757,12 fordelt på 56 834<br>464 aksjer, hver pålydende NOK 0,08.<br><br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Malvin Høydal, mob: +47 97422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Operational update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-06 15:40:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 6. November 2006)<br><br><br>3D seismic<br>The preliminary data interpretation of the 3D seismic down to<br>approximately 2500 meters has been successfully completed. Most<br>importantly, the preliminary 3D seismic interpretation have been used<br>to choose the best possible production zones for wells #103 and #106<br>and to pinpoint the exact location of production zones for Rig #3 in<br>the Petrovsky drilling campaign.<br><br>Preliminary results from 3D:<br><br>  * The preliminary results confirm the information previously issued<br>    in press release August 23rd regarding the increase of the<br>    Tournaisian pay zone from 24 km2 to 54 km2 with accompanying<br>    increase in resources of minimum 20%.<br>  * Preliminary 3D confirms that the East Shaltinsky oil field<br>    extends further to the east in the previously unmapped area<br>    towards the river and the natural geological fault.<br><br><br>SAGA Oil expects that the 3D interpretation including depths below<br>2500 meters will be completed in December. The American SPE Resource<br>Certification company Forrest A Garb & Associates Inc. is<br>continuously being updated as the data becomes available in order to<br>have an official resource certification available as early as<br>possible in 2007. The process of upgrading the extractable resources<br>is how ever an ongoing issue as all data is prepared and produced<br>according to the international SPE standard and requirements.<br><br><br>RIG #1: Continues drilling on well #103 to speed up production start:<br>Rig 1 has currently reached the top of the Tournaisian zone on well<br>#103. Based on the preliminary results from the 3D seismic and in<br>order to speed up production start of the first two wells, it is<br>decided to reschedule the open hole testing of the Tournaisian zone<br>from well #103 to the next well #101. Rig 1 will on well #103 now<br>perform coring of the Tournaisian formation on the way to the<br>targeted depth of about 2250 meters. Start of production is now<br>scheduled to early December for wells #102 and #103.<br><br>RIG #2: Drilling on well #106:<br>Rig #2 has spud-in well #106 and is currently drilling after setting<br>the surface casing at 253 meters. Well #106 is a combined appraisal<br>and production well as it is located on the north eastern perimeter<br>of the East Shaltinsky oil field. It is expected that formation<br>testing and coring will be done on various pay zones on the way down<br>to the targeted total depth.<br><br>RIG #3 option will be exercised:<br>It is decided to exercise the option for a third drilling Rig. The<br>alternative Rig options are currently being evaluated in order to<br>secure a rig contract with the most suitable drilling company. The<br>rig selection process is expected to take 1-2 weeks before final<br>contract is signed. The third Rig will drill the first wells on the<br>Petrovsky oil field. These wells will act as both exploration and<br>production wells for Petrovsky and appraisal wells for East<br>Shaltinsky as the wells will pass through the Tournaisian zone.<br><br>ACCESS ROAD: completed.<br>The access road is completed in time and on budget.<br><br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1086407/189907.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1086407/189907.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Operasjonell oppdatering</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-06 15:40:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 6. november 2006)<br><br><br>3D seismikk<br>Den foreløpige tolking av 3D seismikk for dybder ned til 2500 meter<br>er nå ferdigstilt. Denne foreløpige ferdigstillelsen av 3D data gir<br>selskapet et godt grunnlag for nøyaktig å kunne velge de optimale<br>produksjonssoner for brønnene #103 og #106 og for å kunne<br>identifisere de beste produksjonssonene på Petrovsky feltet for Rigg<br>3.<br><br>Foreløpige resultater fra 3D:<br><br>  * De foreløpige resultater bekrefter den informasjon som selskapet<br>    tidligere har gitt i pressemelding den 23. august angående<br>    økningen av Tournaisian formasjonen fra 24 km2 til 54 km2 og<br>    tilhørende økning i ressurser på minimum 20 %.<br>  * Foreløpige 3D data bekrefter også at Øst Shaltinsky feltet<br>    strekker seg ytterligere mot øst og inn i det tidligere ukjente<br>    området som ligger mot elven og den tilhørende naturlige<br>    geologiske forkastningen.<br><br><br>SAGA Oil forventer at den endelige tolking av 3D inkludert dybder<br>under 2500 meter vil ferdigstilles i løpet av desember. Det<br>amerikanske SPE ressurs sertifiserings selskapet Forrest A Garb &<br>Associates Inc. blir kontinuerlig oppdatert etter hvert som data blir<br>tilgjengelig slik at de kan utstede en offisiell ressurs<br>sertifisering så tidlig som mulig i 2007. Prosessen med å oppgradere<br>de utvinnbare ressursene er for øvrig en prosess som blir forberedt<br>og produsert i henhold til internasjonale SPE krav og standarder.<br><br><br>RIGG #1: Fortsetter å bore brønn #103 for å fremskynde<br>produksjonsstart:<br>Rigg 1 har nå nådd toppen av Tournaisian sonen på brønn #103. Basert<br>på de foreløpige data fra 3D seismikken og for å fremskynde<br>produksjonsstarten for de to første brønnene er det bestemt å flytte<br>åpen hull produksjonstesten av Tournaisian sonen fra brønn #103 til<br>neste brønn #101. Rigg 1 vil nå ta kjerneprøver fra Tournaisian<br>formasjonen i brønn #103 på veien ned til den planlagte dybde på<br>rundt 2250 meter. Produksjonsstart er planlagt til tidlig desember<br>for brønnene #102 og #103.<br><br>RIG #2: Borer på brønn #106:<br>Rigg 2 har startet boring på brønn #106 og borer nå videre etter å ha<br>satt foringsrør på 253 meter. Brønn #106 er en kombinert<br>avgrensningsbrønn og produksjonsbrønn som er lokalisert nordøst på<br>Øst Shaltinsky feltet. Det forventes at formasjonstesting og uttak av<br>kjerneprøver vil gjennomføres ved de ulike produksjonssoner på veien<br>ned til den planlagte totale dybde.<br><br><br>RIGG #3 opsjon vil utøves<br>Det er bestemt å utøve opsjonen på en tredje borerigg. De alternative<br>rigg leverandører blir nå evaluert for å sikre en kontrakt med det<br>selskapet som er best egnet for jobben. Det forventes å ta 1-2 uker<br>før endelig kontrakt er signert. Den tredje riggen vil bore de første<br>brønner ved Petrovsky feltet. Disse brønnene vil både være lete og<br>produksjonsbrønner for Petrovsky feltet samt avgrensningsbrønner for<br>Øst Shaltinsky feltet ettersom brønnene vil passere gjennom<br>Tournaisian sonen.<br><br>VEIBYGGING: ferdigstilt.<br>Veibygging er ferdigstilt til rett tid og innen budsjett.<br><br><br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Malvin Høydal, mob: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Stian Vemmestad, mob: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1086412/189918.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1086412/189918.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Meldepliktig handel</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-03 10:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 3. november 2006) Med henvisning til melding fra 3.<br>november om ferdigstillelse av den rettede emisjon på 18 944 821 nye<br>aksjer i SAGA Oil ASA har følgende innsidere blitt tildelt aksjer i<br>emisjonen:<br><br>Administrerende direktør Malvin Høydal ble tildelt 1 500 000 aksjer<br>gjennom investeringsselskapet MVH Invest AS. MVH Invest AS er et<br>heleid selskap av Malvin Høydal. Etter den siste rettede emisjon har<br>Malvin Høydal 1 500 000 aksjer gjennom MVH Invest AS. I tillegg<br>kontrollerer Malvin Høydal 50,8% av SAGA Petrol AS som totalt eier<br>15 000 000 aksjer i SAGA Oil ASA.<br><br>Styremedlem Karstein Sie ble tildelt 78 000 aksjer gjennom<br>investeringsselskapet Sicom AS. Sicom AS er et heleid selskap av<br>Karstein Sie med familie. Etter den rettede emisjonen eier Karstein<br>Sie 303 000 aksjer og 100 000 warrants gjennom selskapet Sicom AS. I<br>tillegg eier Sie og familien 50% av Årdal Investering AS som eier 100<br>000 aksjer og 17 000 warrants i SAGA Oil ASA. Karstein Sie<br>kontrollerer 13,4% av SAGA Petrol AS som totalt eier 15 000 000<br>aksjer i SAGA Oil ASA.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Notification of trade</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-03 10:10:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 3. November 2006) Reference is made to the November 3<br>notice of the completed private placement of 18 944 821 million new<br>shares in SAGA Oil ASA. The following insiders were allotted shares<br>in the placement:<br><br>CEO Malvin Høydal was allotted 1.500.000 shares through the<br>investment company MVH Invest AS. MVH Invest AS is fully owned by<br>Malvin Høydal. Malvin Høydal will after the private placement own<br>1 500 000 shares through MVH Invest AS. In addition Malvin Høydal<br>owns 50.8% of SAGA Petrol AS which totally holds 15.000.000 shares in<br>SAGA Oil ASA.<br><br>Board member Karstein Sie was allotted 78 000 shares through the<br>investment company Sicom AS. Sicom AS is fully owned by Karstein Sie<br>and his family. After the private placement, Karstein Sie holds 303<br>000 shares and 100 000 warrants through Sicom AS. In addition<br>Karstein Sie and his family owns 50% of Årdal Investering which holds<br>100 000 shares and 17 000 warrants in SAGA Oil ASA. Karstein Sie also<br>own 13,4% of SAGA Petrol AS which totally holds 15 000 000 shares in<br>SAGA Oil ASA.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Financial update: private placement completed</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-03 10:00:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 3. November 2006) Saga Oil ASA is pleased to report that<br>the Private Placement announced on October 17 has been successfully<br>completed. The Private Placement of 18 944 821 shares at a<br>subscription price of NOK 6.00 per share was significantly<br>oversubscribed. The placement was directed towards institutional and<br>private investors. Gross proceeds amount to NOK 113.7 million. The<br>Private Placement was managed by Terra Securities ASA and Carnegie<br>ASA. Completion of the Private Placement is subject to all required<br>regulatory approvals.<br><br>CEO Malvin Høydal says in a comment: We are pleased with the result<br>of this private placement. The net proceeds will bring SAGA Oil into<br>an industrial development phase and it will allow for rapid<br>development of production volumes on the Rodnikovsky license. This<br>last private placement will also limit the future financial risk for<br>the company as the start of production opens up for other types of<br>funding.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Finansiell oppdatering: rettet emisjon ferdigstilt</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-11-03 10:00:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 3. november 2006) Den rettede emisjonen som ble meldt av<br>selskapet 17. oktober er vellykket gjennomført. Den rettede emisjon<br>på 18 944 821 nye aksjer til kurs NOK 6,00 per aksje ble betydelig<br>overtegnet. Emisjonen var rettet mot institusjonelle og private<br>investorer. Brutto proveny var NOK 113,7 millioner. Den rettede<br>emisjonen var tilrettelagt av Terra Securities ASA og Carnegie ASA.<br>Ferdigstillelsen av den rettede emisjonen er underlagt de nødvendige<br>regulatoriske godkjenninger.<br><br>Administrerende direktør Malvin Høydal sier i en kommentar at: Vi er<br>fornøyd med interessen i denne rettede emisjonen. Netto provenyet vil<br>bringe SAGA Oil inn i en industriell utviklingsfase og muliggjør<br>hurtigere produksjonsøkning på Rodnikovsky lisensen. Emisjonen er<br>også viktig for SAGA Oil ettersom den reduserer den fremtidige<br>finansielle risikoen og gir selskapet en produksjon som muliggjør<br>andre finansieringsformer.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Financial update</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-17 09:40:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger October 17. 2006)  In view of the recent encouraging<br>drilling results on the East Shaltinsky oil field and the company's<br>option for a third drilling rig, SAGA Oil ASA is considering a<br>directed share issue of approximately ten to twenty million new<br>shares to finance a fast-track development of our license. Terra<br>Securities ASA and Carnegie ASA have been appointed as managers. It<br>is expected that the process will be finalized by early November.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Finansiell oppdatering</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-17 09:40:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 17. oktober 2006) I lys av de oppløftende bore<br>resultatene på Øst Shaltinsky feltet samt opsjonen for å kunne<br>anvende en tredje bore rigg, vurderer SAGA Oil ASA en rettet emisjon<br>på anslagsvis ti til tjue millioner nye aksjer. Dette for å<br>finansiere en hurtigere utvikling av lisensen. Terra Securities ASA<br>og Carnegie ASA er valgt som tilretteleggere, og det forventes at<br>prosessen skal være ferdigstilt innen begynnelsen av november.<br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Malvin Høydal, mob: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Operasjonell Oppdatering: Boring Startet På Brønn #103</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-09 15:20:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger 9. oktober 2006) Søndag den 8. oktober startet Rigg 1<br>boringen av brønn #103. Som tidligere rapportert, er den foreløpige<br>planen for brønn #103 kun å stoppe for åpen hull produksjonstest av<br>den øvre sonen, Tournaisian, før man borer til den foreløpig satte<br>total dybde på 2246 meter. Produksjonen fra brønn #102 og #103 som er<br>de første brønnene som skal settes i produksjon er planlagt startet<br>tidlig i desember fra Pashiyan sonen i Øst Shaltinsky feltet.<br><br><br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Operational Update: Well #103 Spud-In</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-09 15:20:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger October 9. 2006) October 8, Rig#1 spud-in well #103. As<br>reported earlier, the preliminary plan for well #103 is to stop only<br>for Open Hole production testing of the upper zone, the Tournaisian.<br>Thereafter it is planned to drill down to preliminary set total depth<br>of 2246 meters. Production from wells #102 and #103 which are the<br>first wells to be put in production are expected to start producing<br>by early December from the Pashiyan zone on the East Shaltinsky oil<br>field.<br><br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Produksjonsoppdatering: Rigg Nr.3 Tilgjengelig i 2006</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-06 13:40:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger, 6. oktober 2006) Etter funnet av de tre nye oljebærende<br>lag i Øst Shaltinsky feltet som ble meldt den 4. oktober, har SAGA<br>Oil nå revidert boreprogrammet til også å inkludere muligheten for en<br>3. borerigg. Den alternative planen betyr at det kan<br>produksjonssettes totalt 24 nye brønner innen utgangen av 2007. De to<br>første brønnene vil uansett være i produksjon innen desember 2006.<br><br>Som tidligere rapportert vurderer SAGA fortløpende ulike<br>finansieringsformer for å øke fremdriften på Øst Shaltinsky og<br>Petrovsky feltene. Den endelige beslutning på om man velger å benytte<br>den 3. riggen vil bli tatt innen slutten av oktober/begynnelsen av<br>desember.<br><br>De umiddelbare planene for de tre riggene er: Rigg 1 starter boring<br>på brønn #103 ved Pad 1 innen uke 41. Rigg 2 forventes å starte<br>boring på den første brønnen på Pad 2 i løpet av uke 42. Rigg nummer<br>3 (opsjon) kan starte boring på det nye Petrovsky feltet innen<br>utgangen av året.<br><br>Brønnene #102 og #103 er de første to brønnene som skal<br>produksjonssettes, og det forventes at produksjonen fra disse starter<br>innen desember fra Pashiyan sonen på Øst Shaltinsky feltet.<br><br><br>RIGG #1: Borestart brønn #103 på Pad 1 innen uke 41.<br><br>  * Rigg #1 forventes å starte boring på den neste brønn #103 innen<br>    uke 41.<br>  * Den foreløpige plan for brønn #103 er å bare stoppe boringen for<br>    å teste den øvre sonen, Tournaisian. Det vil da bli en åpent hull<br>    test for å bestemme gjennomstrømningskapasitet (flow capasity).<br>    Deretter er det planlagt å bore ned til den foreløpige totale<br>    dybde på 2246 meter.<br>  * Det vil benyttes et optimalisert boreprogram som er basert på<br>    erfaringene fra brønn #102. Derfor forventes det at boretiden<br>    reduseres til ca en måned, avhengig av tiden det tar for åpen<br>    hull testing.<br>  * Produksjon fra de første to brønnene (#102 og #103) på Pad 1<br>    forventes å starte i løpet av desember.<br><br><br>RIGG #2: Borestart for første brønn på Pad 2 i løpet av uke 42.<br><br>  * Rigg 2 er montert, og gjennomgår nå forberedende vedlikehold for<br>    å være klar til å starte boring på den første brønnen på Pad 2 i<br>    løpet av uke 42.<br>  * Brønnen vil bli boret forbi den laveste produksjonssonen<br>    (Pashiyan) til en foreløpig total dybde på 2300 meter.<br>  * Målsonen for den første brønnen som bores av Rigg 2 er den nye<br>    produksjonssonen (lavere) og den opprinnelige Pashiyan<br>    sandsteinsformasjonen på de lavere nivåer.<br><br><br>RIGG #3 (Opsjon) kan starte boring på det nye Petrovsky feltet i<br>løpet av 2006<br><br>  * Som et resultat av de positive initielle bore resultater vurderer<br>    nå SAGA Oil å benytte en tredje bore rigg for å fremskynde<br>    utviklingen av Øst Shaltinsky og Petrovsky feltet. Den tredje<br>    riggen er tilgjengelig til å starte boring av en letebrønn og<br>    fire produksjonsbrønner på Petrovsky feltet. Den første brønnen<br>    vil også være en avgrensningsbrønn for Øst Shaltinsky feltet<br>    ettersom foreløpige resultater indikerer at Øst Shaltinsky feltet<br>    forlenges inn i Petrovsky feltet.<br>  * SAGA kan da komplettere en ny klynge med 5 brønner på Petrovsky<br>    feltet innen sommeren 2007. Disse brønnene kan deretter settes i<br>    produksjon. Den 3. riggen kan deretter flyttes til Øst Shaltinsky<br>    feltet for å fortsette med produksjonsboring der.<br><br><br>LISENSOPPDATERING: Betalt for gammel seismikk og feltdata<br>SAGA Oil's datterselskap, PROMGEOTEK LLC, betalte den 25. september<br>$350 000 for kostnader relatert til bruk av gammel seismikk og<br>feltdata på Øst Shaltinsky feltet. Kostnaden er definert av<br>Ministeriet for Økonomi og Ministeriet for Natur Ressurser i<br>Russland. Dette er en viktig milepæl, og det resterende arbeidet som<br>er nødvendig før lisensen kan utstedes er av mer byråkratisk karakter<br>noe som ikke burde ta mer enn to til tre uker.<br><br>3 D SEISMIKK: Tolking er forventet å være klar i oktober<br>Den foreløpige tolking av 3D seismikken er forventet å være klar ved<br>utgangen av oktober / begynnelsen av november måned.<br><br>VEIBYGGING: Forventes ferdigstilt innen 15. oktober.<br>Ferdigstillelsen av den 11 meter brede og 3,2 km lange veien som<br>bygges fra hovedveien gjennom Øst Shaltinsky feltet forventes å være<br>ferdigstilt innen 15. oktober i god tid før den første frosten.<br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1079854/186706.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1079854/186706.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA Oil ASA - Operational update: Rig #3 option available</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-06 13:40:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>(Stavanger October 6. 2006) Due to the discovery of the three new pay<br>zones at the East Shaltinsky oil field which was reported in press<br>release October 4., SAGA Oil has now revised the drilling programme<br>to include the option of a 3.rd Drilling Rig.  The alternative plan<br>means that a total of 24 wells could be in production by the end of<br>2007. The first two wells will regardless be in production by<br>December 2006.<br><br>As reported, SAGA continuously evaluates further funding solutions to<br>increase progress on the East Shaltinsky and Petrovsky oil fields.<br>Decision on whether to use a third Drilling Rig will be made within<br>end of October/early November.<br><br>Immediate plans for the Rigs are: Rig 1 is expected to spud well #103<br>on Pad 1 within week 41. Rig no 2 is expected to spud the first well<br>on Pad 2 during week 42. Rig no 3 (option) could start drilling on<br>the new Petrovsky oil field within 2006.<br><br>Wells #102 and #103 which are the first wells to be put in production<br>are expected to start producing by early December from the Pashiyan<br>zone on the East Shaltinsky oil field.<br><br>RIG #1: Spuds well #103 on Pad 1 within week 41.<br><br>  * Rig # 1 is expected to spud the next well # 103 within week 41.<br>  * The preliminary plan for well #103 is to stop only for testing of<br>    the upper zone, the Tournaisian, which will be tested in Open<br>    Hole in order to determine flow capacity. Thereafter it is<br>    planned to drill down to preliminary set total depth of 2246<br>    meters.<br>  * The well will be drilled using an optimized drilling program<br>    based on the experience from well #102. Therefore drilling time<br>    is estimated to be close to one month, pending the required time<br>    for open hole testing.<br>  * Production from the first two wells (#102 and #103) on Pad 1 is<br>    expected to commence during December.<br><br><br>RIG #2: Spuds first well on Pad 2 during week 42.<br><br>  * Rig 2 is assembled, and is expected to complete pre-spudding<br>    maintenance in order to be ready to spud the first well on Pad 2<br>    during week 42.<br>  * The well will be drilled past the lowest production zone<br>    (Pashiyan) to a preliminary TD of 2300 meters.<br>  * Target zone for the first well drilled by Rig 2 is the new lower<br>    production zone and the initial Pashiyan sandstone formation on<br>    the lower level.<br><br><br>RIG #3 (Option) ready to start drilling on the new Petrovsky oil<br>field in 2006.<br><br>  * As a result of initial drilling results, SAGA Oil has included<br>    the possibility for a third drilling Rig to ramp up the<br>    development programme of the East Shaltinsky and the Petrovsky<br>    oil fields. The third Rig could therefore start up the drilling<br>    of the first exploration well and four production wells on the<br>    Petrovsky oil field. The first well will also be an appraisal<br>    well for the East Shaltinsky field as initial data indicates that<br>    the East Shaltinsky oil field extends into the Petrovsky field.<br>  * SAGA's revised plan calls for completing a new cluster of 5 wells<br>    on the Petrovsky oil field by summer 2007 which is thereafter put<br>    on production. The 3'rd drilling rig will then move to the East<br>    Shaltinsky oil field to continue with production drilling there.<br><br><br>LICENSE UPDATE: Paid for old seismic and field data<br>The SAGA Oil ASA subsidiary, PROMGEOTEK LLC, paid on September 25'th<br>the amount of $ 350 000 for costs related to the use of old seismic<br>and field data for the East Shaltinsky oil field, as defined by the<br>Ministry of Economy and the Ministry of Natural Resources of Russia.<br>The remaining part of work required before the license will be issued<br>is of more bureaucratic character, but should not require more than<br>about two/three weeks.<br><br>3 D SEISMIC: Interpretation expected to be completed by late October<br>The preliminary interpretation is expected to be completed by end of<br>October/ beginning of November.<br><br>ACCESS ROAD: Expected to be finished within October 15.<br>The completion of the 11 meters wide and 3,2 km long access road<br>which is being built from the main road and across the East<br>Shaltinsky oil field is expected to be completed by October 15th in<br>good time before the first frost.<br><br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://hugin.info/137028/R/1079863/186707.pdf">
http://hugin.info/137028/R/1079863/186707.pdf</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Well 102. Saga discovers 3 new production zones</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-06 11:25:19</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p></p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/5153.pdf">
Well 102. Saga discovers 3 new production zones.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Bronn #102: Saga oppdager 3 nye produksjonssoner</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-06 11:24:41</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p></p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/5152.pdf">
Bronn 102. Saga oppdager 3 nye produksjonssoner.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Well #102: Saga discovers 3 new production zones</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-04 17:10:01</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>The well #102 is now successfully drilled, cored and logged to the<br>desired total depth of 2064 meters. The cost of drilling was within<br>budget. All logging data has been correlated and done according to<br>western standards and will be part of the basis for the next SPE<br>adjustment of resources.<br><br>Three new oil bearing zones in the East Shaltinsky field have been<br>discovered as a result of successful drilling, coring and logging.<br>Based on preliminary results, one of the three new zones (Middle<br>Devon Zhivetsky) is currently deemed producible. This new producible<br>zone is situated close to the "Pashiyan" zone and has good oil<br>quality. This discovery increases the possibility of well completion<br>using dual production from both the lower zones (Pashiyan and the new<br>zone). The new zone is to be tested during completion of well #102<br>and/or well #103 by November/December.<br><br>Orenburg region has other oil fields with pay zones that is analogue<br>with SAGA's newly discovered Middle Devon Zhivetsky which has yielded<br>from 80 to 2000 BOPD by own production pressure.<br><br>In light of the encouraging results, SAGA continuously evaluates<br>further funding solutions to increase progress on the East Shaltinsky<br>and Petrovsky oil fields.<br><br>Whether the two other new zones are producible will depend on further<br>results from core analysis, 3D and future well testing.<br><br>SEDIMENTOLOGY OF THE 3 NEW PAY ZONES<br><br>1. Fammenian fractured limestone formation:<br>a. Porosity: 7-8%<br>b. Permeability: fractured limestone<br>c. - Total thickness of oil saturation zone: 18,9 m<br>    - Total effective thickness of oil saturated zone:  5,2 m<br>d. Oil saturation factor: 62%<br><br>2. Upper Devonian Fransky fractured limestone formation:<br>a. Porosity: under laboratory investigation<br>b. Permeability: fractured limestone formation<br>c. - Total thickness of oil saturation zone: 15,0 m<br>    - Total effective thickness of oil saturated zone: 3,1 m<br>d. Oil saturation factor: under laboratory investigation<br><br>3. Middle Devon Zhivetsky sandstone formation [PRODUCIBLE]:<br>a. Porosity: 15-19%<br>b. Permeability: 300-450 millidarcy<br>c.- Total thickness of oil saturation zone: 3,2 m<br>   - Total effective thickness of oil saturated zone: 1,9 m<br>d. Oil saturation factor: 65%<br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Mr. Malvin Høydal, cell: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Mr. Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Brønn #102: Saga oppdager 3 nye produksjonssoner</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-10-04 17:00:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Brønn #102 er nå ferdigstilt med boring, kjerneprøvetaking og logging<br>til den ønskede totale dybde på 2064 meter. Operasjonen var en<br>suksess, og innen budsjett. Alle loggedata fra brønnen er innhentet<br>og ferdigstilt i henhold til vestlig standard, og vil danne grunnlag<br>for den neste SPE justeringen av resurssene.<br><br>Som et resultat av den vellykkede boring, kjerneprøvetaking og<br>logging er det oppdaget tre nye oljebærende soner på Øst Shaltinsky<br>feltet. Basert på foreløpige resultater er en av disse tre nye sonene<br>produserbar (Middle Devon Zhivetsky). Denne nye produserbare sonen er<br>lokalisert nær den eksisterende Pashiyan sonen og har god<br>oljekvalitet. Funnet av denne sonen øker muligheten for<br>brønnkomplettering med produksjon fra både den lavere sonen Pashiyan<br>og den nye sonen. Den nye sonen skal ytterligere testes ved<br>kompletteringen av brønn #102 og/eller brønn #103 innen<br>november/desember 2006.<br><br>I Orenburg regionen produserer oljefelt med oljebærende soner<br>tilsvarende Middle Devon Zhivetsky som SAGA har oppdaget fra 80 til<br>2000 fat per dag ved hjelp av eget trykk.<br><br>I lys av de oppløftende resultatene vurderer selskapet fortløpende<br>ulike finansieringsløsninger for å øke fremdriften på feltene Øst<br>Shaltinsky og Petrovsky.<br><br>Hvorvidt de to øvrige nye sonene er produserbare vil avhenge av<br>ytterligere resultater fra kjerneprøve analyser, 3D og fremtidig<br>brønntesting.<br><br><br>SEDIMENT OVERSIKT FOR DE 3 NYE SONENE<br><br>1. Fammenian fractured limestone formation:<br>a. Porøsitet: 7-8%<br>b. Permeabilitet: fractured limestone<br>c. - Total tykkelse på oljebærende sone: 18,9 m<br>    - Total effektiv tykkelse på oljebærende sone: 5,2 m<br>d. Olje metningsgrad faktor: 62%<br><br>2. Upper Devonian Fransky fractured limestone formation:<br>a. Porøsitet: undersøkes i laboratorium<br>b. Permeabilitet: fractured limestone formation<br>c. - Total tykkelse på oljebærende sone: 15,0 m<br>    - Total effektiv tykkelse på oljebærende sone: 3,1 m<br>d. Olje metningsgrad faktor: undersøkes i laboratorium<br><br>3. Middle Devon Zhivetsky sandstone formation [PRODUSERBAR]:<br>a. Porøsitet: 15-19%<br>b. Permeabilitet: 300-450 millidarcy<br>c.  - Total tykkelse på oljebærende sone: 3,2 m<br>     - Total effektiv tykkelse på oljebærende sone: 1,9 m<br>d. Olje metningsgrad faktor: 65%<br><br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst kontakt<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CEO Malvin Høydal, mob: +47 47422959, email:<br>malvin.hoeydal@sagaoil.no<br>SAGA Oil ASA - CFO Stian Vemmestad, cell: +47 92805787, email:<br>sve@sagaoil.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA proves success with revitalisation of well No.100</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-09-12 11:27:56</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>The first well No. 100 is revitalised with success:<br>Well number 100 is an old well drilled by the previous owners. The well was initially classified by SAGA Oil as a lost well due to improper drilling and completion methods. However, due to implementation of SAGA Oil well stimulation programme, the well is now revitalized. Well 100 was under the initial re-opening and testing yielding a commercial test production of 180 bbl/day of oil with no water content. <br><br>Drilling of well No. 102 has reached depth of 2244 meters:<br>Well number 102 is the first well drilled under SAGA supervision on the East Shaltinsky field. The well has now reached the final total measured depth of 2244 meters. Currently the well is undergoing open hole logging before running in and cementing the production casing, in order to commence with production testing of targeted zones and final well completion for production.<br><br>Information from coring and testing of lower pay zones:<br>The interpretation and testing of the core samples from the pay zones below the Tournaisian is still ongoing.<br> <br>For additional information please see the attached document.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/5023.pdf">
Saga press release 12 09 061_EN.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA lykkes med revitalisering av brønn 100</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-09-12 11:26:32</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>SAGA Oil lykkes med revitalisering av brønn no. 100:<br>Brønn nummer 100 er en brønn som ble boret av de tidligere eiere. Brønnen ble opprinnelig klassifisert som tapt av SAGA Oil grunnet mangelfulle boring og kompletteringsmetoder fra de tidligere eiere. Etter gjennomføring av SAGA Oils brønn stimuleringsprogram har selskapet nå klart å revitalisere brønnen. Etter gjenåpning og testing har nå brønn Nr. 100   klart å produsere 180 fat/dag olje uten vann innhold.<br><br>Status på boring av brønn no 102<br>Brønn 102 er den første brønn i Øst Shaltinsky feltet som er boret under ledelse av SAGA Oil. Brønnen har nå nådd sin totale målte lengde av 2244 meter. For tiden gjennomgår brønnen åpent hull logging, og det planlegges deretter å kjøre inn produksjons foringsrøret og sementering slik at det er mulig å starte produksjonstesting og endelig brønnferdigstillelse.<br><br>Informasjon fra kjerneboring og testing av lavere oljebærende lag:<br>Tolking og testing av kjerneprøver fra lavere oljebærende lag under Tournaisian pågår fremdeles.<br><br>For ytterligere informasjon, vennligst se vedlagte dokument.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/5022.pdf">
Saga press release 12 09 061_NO.pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA increases the resources of the Tournaisian pay zone</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-08-23 16:07:05</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>SAGA increases the resources of the Tournaisian pay zone.<br><br>Drilling of well no 102, which is the first well drilled under Saga supervision on the East Shaltinsky oil field, has reached 1880 meters. Total depth to be drilled is 2050 meters. <br><br>Based on the results from the drilling there is now available new information for the Tournaisian pay zone located at 1242,5 meters depth:<br>*	Increased acreage of the oil saturated pay zone from 24 km2 to 54 km2 area<br>*	Oil resources increase minimum 20%<br>*	Oil saturation factor increases up to a content of 56 %  of oil saturation<br><br>The coring and testing of the pay zones below the Tournaisian is ongoing and the preliminary results are expected to be available in about 2 weeks time.<br><br>Update:<br>The new coring of the Tournaisian has given a more accurate redefinition of the level for water-oil contact from 1247,5 meters down to 1253 meters depth which increases the acreage of oil saturated pay zone from 24 km2 to approximately 54 km2. <br>The Tournaisian oil saturated pay zone is thereby extended and reaches into Saga's second oil field, the Petrovsky oil field on the south end of the licensed area.<br>Reserves of the Tournaisian pay zone are expected to increase accordingly with a minimum of 20%, the more exact increase of the resources will be determined after the interpretation of the 3D seismic.<br>The oil saturation factor for the Tournaisian is now approximately 56% which is 6% higher then previously reported.  <br>Saga expects to finalize drilling and production testing of well no 102 by mid-September.<br><br>Saga is currently mobilizing a second drilling rig on East Shaltinsky for drilling on pad no.2. The rig is expected to spud well no. 106 by mid-September and is contracted from one of the Gasprom Drilling divisions.<br><br>The development of infrastructure for the oil field is on going and the high voltage line is now completed and in operation, construction of the new11 meter wide access road is about 25% completed.<br><br>The 3D data collection has been almost completed and we expect first interpretation of data by early October. <br><br>Malvin Høydal, CEO of Saga Oil comments: "We are very pleased to receive test data that exceed our expectations for the East Shaltinsky oil field and specifically increasing of the Tournaisian zone which is the largest. <br>The new results increase the thickness of the Tournaisian pay Zone by 3,4 meter from 9,4 meter to 12,8 meter which will result in increased productivity and simplifies the well completion.<br>The test well drilled by the previous owners was unsuccessful in regards of getting accurate data, this was however largely due to lack of proper drilling procedures and control. The current new data from our new well confirm our view that value creation is easily achievable by implementing proper procedures and control throughout the field operation".<br><br><br>For further information please contact Mr. Malvin Hoeydal, President and CEO<br>                                                <br>      Contact information:         <br>Telephone: +47 51 63 08 00,   <br>Mobile telephone: +47 97 422 959,   <br>Facsimile: +47 51 63 07 99</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/4917.doc">
Saga press release 23.08.06.doc</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA completes a mNOK 100 bond issue</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-07-17 13:01:02</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Saga Oil has completed a mNOK 100 bond issue. The bond carries 12 % interest and matures July 14, 2008. In addition, the bond investors have received 3.4 million separate warrants, corresponding to an approx. 1/3 bond conversion ratio. The warrants have an exercise price of NOK 8.00 per share and can be exercised at any time up to July 14, 2008. Saga has applied for admission for trading of the warrants on the OTC list.<br><br> <br>For further information please contact Mr. Malvin Hoeydal, President and CEO</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>SAGA spudding the first production well on East-Shaltinsky oilfield</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-07-04 16:18:28</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Malvin Hoeydal, President and CEO of SAGA Oil ASA comments:<br>“We are very pleased to announce that we have spudded in the first production well on the East-Shaltinsky oilfield, as it signifies the rapid development since SAGA Oil acquired the management and operational control of the Rodnikovsky license in March this year.<br><br>This first well will be drilled to the total depth of around 2200 meters with up to 45 deg. deviation in order to reach the thickest interval of the first production zone, whereupon it will be drilled further in sub-vertical trajectory in order to optimise the data from the extensive coring and well testing programme throughout the 3 production zones.<br>We expect to have this first well drilled to TD and cased in 45 to 60 days. Modern western technology and practices will be utilized in order to collect, interpret and analyse all the necessary data needed for further assessment of resources and improve and optimise drilling technology for the program which is in extent of 35 additional production wells.<br>The successful completion of this first well together with the now 75% completed field work for 3D seismic and its interpretation will further increase the proven and possible resources of the East-Shaltinsky oil field”.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
